Vic Grigoryev (vgrigory)

Instructions: Run the following commands to obtain the outfile
make clean (<- optional)
make pipeit
./pipeit
cat outfile

Notes:
- outfile will not show up when running for the first time since it is created after the ls command
is run. If you want it to be there then run the program again.
- I've included -D_XOPEN_SOURCE = 700 because otherwise -Wimplicit-function-declaration would give
me a warning for fileno at line 88. I've included stdio.h I don't know what else it wants and I've
read this as a fix on StackOverflow and it works so it will stay.

- i apologize in advance for the photo (a little bit)
- this took me so long because i didnt realize the children just had to run execl. this was so easy.
i spent HOURS sitting on this wondering why it didnt work. and i also just realized that you can set
the file descriptor after opening it as the stdout via dup2 instead of using a while loop to write
to it from ANOTHER pipe via the parent. c is so easy when you actually know how to think correctly.
dup2 is awesome
